00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:03.220
But I'm not sure I know what I can do for her.

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:18.610
The Sagittarius is sinking further and further
into the darkness of uncertainty.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:23.740
The key to get out from
the darkness is Aquarius' girl.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.690
Say, Marion.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.300
About this afternoon...

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:43.600
If you're talking about a trampoline, don't worry.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.970
I'm not interested in trampolines at all.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.670
Marion, do you remember Mom's shows?

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.550
She was so pretty.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:17:00.250
She looked like a bird which flies the sky freely.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:05.560
I loved to watch your mom
when she was on the trampoline.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.360
Dad...

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.020
I have something I want to show you, Marion.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.710
Look at this.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.370
What?

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:36.720
Dad... This is...

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.720
It's your mom's stage notebook.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:45.360
I'm sorry for hiding it from you.
I thought it would make you sad.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.700
Mom's...

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:52.830
This is the notebook your mom used to jot down
her ideas when they came to mind.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:58.400
Then she used to practice over and over
until she could do them.

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:04.310
"Marion's Debut Show"...

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.420
That's right.

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:09.060
Your mom would come up with
performance ideas,

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.180
and I'd come up with
staging ideas.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.430
I remember we'd talk about it every day,

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:17.230
and even quarrel every once in a while.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:25.930
To appear on stage with you and do a
trampoline act was your mom's dream.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.180
Mama...

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:32.010
I want to...

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:39.080
I want to jump on the trampoline
onstage with you too...

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.380
Marion...

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:50.560
When I heard that you were jumping
on the trampoline, I was happy.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.370
I'm sure your mom feels the same way.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:58.540
Mom too?

00:18:58.540 --> 00:18:59.530
Yeah.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.910
You like the trampoline, don't you, Marion?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.810
Yes.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.810
Then, for your mom's sake,
I want you to grow to like it even more.

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:13.320
Yes.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:16.120
Wow, amazing. This is good.

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:17.930
Yeah, it looks fun.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.930
It's perfect for the image of the Kids' Stage too!

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.790
I want to do that one.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.970
Yeah, I think it's a really good idea too.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.640
Isn't this great, Marion?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.770
Yeah.

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.270
Hey, what we're going to do
about Cynthia's role?

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.170
Oh... Well...

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:35.840
Sora, will you do it for me?

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:38.110
What?! Me?

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:39.280
You don't want to?

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.420
No, it's not like that.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:43.050
You don't mind me doing it?

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.140
Yep. I want you to do it.

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.680
Then I'll take up your kind offer and do it!

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:51.130
Yeah!

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.660
Wow, things are getting exciting!

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.060
Does this mean I'm going to pair with Jonathan?

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:58.730
Oh, it could be a good idea.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.170
Jonathan, let's do our best.

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:16.040
PEEP!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.680
Here!

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.850
They laughed...

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:26.990
Okay, Jonathan, say hello to everyone!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.330
Ready? Go!

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.830
Good boy.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:34.860
That looks good on you, Marion.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:54.050
This is the place where my mom was.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.590
Ready? Jump!

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:34.290
Jump!

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:36.660
I wonder why it is...

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:38.470
When someone performs with Sora,

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.370
they always start smiling.

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:43.300
Marion...

00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:50.940
This is what they went against me to create?

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:56.140
How frivolous.

00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:58.510
Leon, wait.

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:13.500
Everyone is smiling.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:16.370
This is the real Kaleido Stage.

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:27.340
Maybe this is the Kaleido Stage
I'm aiming for. Maybe! Maybe!

